WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.410
In April 2018, the UK put a new levy

2
00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.430
on sugary soft drinks.

3
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.820
At the start, the sugariest
drinks were charged 24

4
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.690
pence for every litre.

5
00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.370
And the law charged it to
the companies that make them,

6
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.770
not to shoppers.

7
00:00:14.770 --> 00:00:17.350
But a company can raise its prices.

8
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.900
And shoppers can switch to something else.

9
00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:22.580
So when a tax is charged to sellers,

10
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.820
who really ends up paying it?

11
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.140
In this mission, you'll shift
the supply curve by the tax

12
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.740
and shade the part each side carries.

13
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:33.270
Then you'll make a
prediction in a graph lab,

14
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:35.540
move a slider, and test it.

15
00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.080
Your mission: find out
who really pays the tax.
